File: vUX-formComponents.js

=======================================================================
Section 1 — datePicker: scroll button creation
OLD_SECTION
var previousButtonElement = $$.ce("BUTTON", {class:"linactive vPrev", id:"vPrev", type:"button"});
...
var nextButtonElement = $$.ce("BUTTON", {class:"rinactive vNext", id:"vNext", type:"button"});

NEW_SECTION
var previousButtonElement = $$.ce("BUTTON", {class:"vPrev vListBt vListBt-Left sInactive", id:"vPrev", type:"button"});
...
var nextButtonElement = $$.ce("BUTTON", {class:"vNext vListBt vListBt-Right sInactive", id:"vNext", type:"button"});

REASON
ListScroller's delegated click handler only responds to elements carrying
vListBt + vListBt-Left/vListBt-Right; the buttons never had those classes, so the
decade-series prev/next buttons were dead. The initial inactive look now uses the
shared sInactive class that ListScroller actually toggles (see Section 2).

=======================================================================
Section 2 — datePicker: toggleListScroller() configuration
OLD_SECTION
listControllerObj.config.buttons = [LeftBt, RightBt];
listControllerObj.config.inactiveButtonsClassName = ["off"];
listControllerObj.config.effects = [0.4, "cubic-bezier(0,.99,0,1)"];
listControllerObj.config.inactiveButtonsClassName = ["linactive", "rinactive"];
listControllerObj.config.scrollSize = 300
listControllerObj.config.paddingRight = 0;
listControllerObj.config.spaceError = 2;

NEW_SECTION
listControllerObj.config.buttons = [LeftBt, RightBt];
listControllerObj.config.inactiveButtonClassName = "sInactive"; //one shared class; the arrows' CSS keys off .vPrev/.vNext
listControllerObj.config.scrollSize = 300
listControllerObj.config.paddingRight = 0;

REASON
Discovered by driving the new example: opening any date picker with a decade-series
view threw "Setup error: Buttons class for inactive state not specified" — which also
aborted showDateBox before setSuperActive, breaking the open picker's z-index raise.
ListScroller's property is inactiveButtonClassName (singular, string); the plural
array assignments silently did nothing, and config.effects / config.spaceError do not
exist on ListScroller at all (removed).

=======================================================================
Section 3 — all six builders: generated stylesheet selector specificity
OLD_SECTION
Generated rules were emitted as ".v<className> ..." (select/radio/checkbox/
slideSwitch/file) and ".vDateIcon..." / ".vDatePicker .vSelected" (datePicker), e.g.:
css += ".v" + radioClassName + " .selected::before {" + selectedStyle + "}";
css += ".vDatePicker .vSelected{" + selectionStyle + "}";

NEW_SECTION
Generated rules are now anchored to the wrapper base class the widget already carries,
e.g.:
css += ".vRadioButtonWrapper.v" + radioClassName + " .selected::before {" + selectedStyle + "}";
css += ".vDatePicker .vDateBoxTool .vSelected{" + selectionStyle + "}";
(select → .vSelect.v<name>, radio → .vRadioButtonWrapper.v<name>, checkbox →
.vCheckboxWrapper.v<name>, slideSwitch → .vSlideSwitchWrapper.v<name>, file →
.vFile.v<name>, datePicker → .vDatePicker .dFieldCon .vDateIcon... /
.vDatePicker .vDateBoxTool .vSelected)

REASON
The static formComponents.css <link> is appended after the generated <style> elements
(the asset-path bootstrap is async), so at equal specificity the static defaults win
every tie and configured styles silently fail for any property the static sheet also
declares. Confirmed live in the example: selectedRadioStyle's blue rendered black
(static .selected::before background-color won), the checkbox checkedCheckboxStyle
content glyph never appeared (static content:'' won), and the file inputButton
background lost to the static gradient. Raising the generated selectors' specificity
by one class makes explicitly-configured styles override defaults — the documented
contract — without reordering any stylesheets.
